 "notes": [
  "Cracow (Bohemian in 1300) was held by Przemysł II of Greater Poland from 1290 until Wenceslaus II took it later in 1291; Sandomierz, Sieradz, Łęczyca and Brześć Kujawski were Władysław the Elbow-high's (our sandomierz).",
  "Oppeln: Bolko I and his brothers did homage to Wenceslaus II on 17 January 1291, after the start date, so they are sovereign on 1 January.",
  "Galicia-Volhynia was split in 1291 between Lev I (Galicia) and Mstislav Danylovych (Volhynia).",
  "Wallachia (Hungarian dependency in Euratlas) has no realm of ours: the voivodes of 1291 (Bărbat) are thinly attested; a gap. Moldavia between Carpathians and Dniester lay under Nogai's Tatars.",
  "The Prussian and Livonian branches of the Teutonic Order are one entity in Euratlas; Semigallia (conquered 1290) and Sudovia (1283) are labelled as peoples there and given to the orders here.",
  "Caralis and Gallura were Pisan in 1291 (Cagliari Pisan since 1258, Gallura annexed 1288); Logudoro was split between Genoa, the Doria and Sassari, left to the spread.",
  "Italian city lordships of 1300 we do not model (Alessandria, Asti, Bergamo, Brescia, Como, Cremona, Lodi, Novara, Parma, Pavia, Piacenza, Tortona, Pistoia, Volterra and others) are left to the spread: a gap."
